  "name": "Monitor ad campaign health daily with Spendict diagnosis and Slack alerts",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e6ea5873-911c-45f5-b9b1-e1fd8547ddaf",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Monitor ad campaign health daily\n\nReads your live campaign metrics from Google Sheets each morning, has Spendict diagnose every campaign, and alerts Slack the moment one needs attention — with the exact bottleneck named.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A daily schedule reads every campaign row from your metrics sheet.\n2. A Code node shapes each row into a diagnosis request, coercing numbers and dropping blanks.\n3. Spendict's `analyze_campaign_performance` scores the funnel against platform and objective benchmarks and names the single biggest bottleneck.\n4. A Switch routes on the verdict: `healthy` and `insufficient_data` are logged quietly, `fix_first` and `kill_or_rebuild` are logged and alerted.\n5. Every campaign lands in a dated health log, so you can watch trends over time.\n\n### Setup\n\n- **Google Sheets** — connect Google on both Sheets nodes. The metrics sheet needs headers such as `campaign`, `platform`, `objective`, `spend`, `impressions`, `ctr`, `conversions`, `cpa`, `roas` (any subset works). The log sheet receives `campaign`, `platform`, `verdict`, `bottleneck`, `diagnosis`, `checked_at`.\n- **Spendict** — free key at spendict.com/dashboard, then Header Auth `Authorization: Bearer spd_live_…` on the Spendict node.\n- **Slack** — paste your Incoming Webhook URL into the Slack node.\n- **Schedule** — defaults to 08:00 daily; change it on the trigger.\n\n### Customization tips\n\nSwap Google Sheets for your warehouse or ad-platform node. Delete the Slack node to log silently."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
